1
00:01:41,780 --> 00:01:48,860
[Genius Girlfriend]

2
00:01:49,250 --> 00:01:51,850
[Episode 11]

3
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:55,920
What's this?

4
00:01:56,150 --> 00:01:57,880
It's a semi-automatic guitar.

5
00:01:58,070 --> 00:02:00,310
Just press the corresponding keys
and it'll play the chords.

6
00:02:00,310 --> 00:02:01,120
Give it a try.

7
00:02:02,230 --> 00:02:03,230
That's so cool.

8
00:02:03,790 --> 00:02:04,760
Let me try.

9
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:16,910
My fingers are so sensitive.
Don't even mention pressing down

10
00:02:16,910 --> 00:02:20,170
on the strings—
just lightly touching one hurts like hell.

11
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:24,560
These fingers are pretty much done for.

12
00:02:26,710 --> 00:02:28,170
I brought some band-aids.

13
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:32,520
Give me your hand.

14
00:02:42,310 --> 00:02:43,440
Let me do it instead.

15
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:55,970
Does it hurt?

16
00:02:56,910 --> 00:02:57,910
Be gentle.

17
00:03:10,460 --> 00:03:12,580
Can we really count on Duan Qiyan?

18
00:03:13,530 --> 00:03:14,790
We'll have to go for it.

19
00:03:17,090 --> 00:03:19,210
It's all or nothing then.

20
00:03:20,579 --> 00:03:21,370
Let's do it.

21
00:04:47,570 --> 00:04:50,300
Baihui, are the monthly exam results
not out yet?

22
00:04:51,390 --> 00:04:54,540
[Daily Study Plan]

23
00:04:51,980 --> 00:04:54,130
My colleague Zhang's son is also
in No. 1 High School.

24
00:04:54,130 --> 00:04:56,330
He said the results came out
a long time ago.

25
00:04:56,330 --> 00:04:57,130
They're out.

26
00:04:58,860 --> 00:05:00,250
I didn't do very well this time,

27
00:05:00,250 --> 00:05:01,650
so I didn't tell you guys.

28
00:05:03,190 --> 00:05:04,390
What rank did you get?

29
00:05:05,860 --> 00:05:06,660
I got...

30
00:05:07,930 --> 00:05:08,740
Fifth.

31
00:05:09,250 --> 00:05:10,220
Fifth?

32
00:05:17,150 --> 00:05:19,720
[Daily Study Plan]

33
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:22,330
What's this?

34
00:05:23,770 --> 00:05:24,620
Lyrics.

35
00:05:24,690 --> 00:05:26,370
You got fifth place and you still
have time for this kind of stuff?

36
00:05:26,370 --> 00:05:29,770
- No, this is my...
- Does this have anything to do with studying?

37
00:05:29,770 --> 00:05:31,370
Are you spending all day at school

38
00:05:31,370 --> 00:05:33,060
thinking about these pointless things?

39
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:34,100
No, I just...

40
00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:35,360
Don't bother arguing.

41
00:05:35,510 --> 00:05:36,810
I'll go talk to
your homeroom teacher tomorrow

42
00:05:36,810 --> 00:05:38,450
and find out what's really going on.

43
00:05:38,450 --> 00:05:39,220
Tomo...

44
00:05:39,690 --> 00:05:40,330
Dad!

45
00:05:50,230 --> 00:05:55,690
[Celebrating the Anniversary
of Nanhai No. 1 High School]

46
00:05:59,060 --> 00:05:59,860
Ms. Kong.

47
00:06:00,370 --> 00:06:02,220
Jin Baihui's grades

48
00:06:02,220 --> 00:06:04,050
have dropped way too much this time.

49
00:06:04,050 --> 00:06:06,220
We're having a hard time accepting it.

50
00:06:07,930 --> 00:06:09,770
Fluctuations in grades are normal.

51
00:06:09,770 --> 00:06:10,500
We don't need to

52
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:12,540
let a single set of results get to us.

53
00:06:13,130 --> 00:06:14,370
Besides, I don't think

54
00:06:14,370 --> 00:06:17,030
the drop is necessarily
as serious as you think.

55
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:17,770
Well...

56
00:06:19,010 --> 00:06:20,420
A drop is a drop.

57
00:06:20,420 --> 00:06:22,820
Does it matter
whether it's serious or not?

58
00:06:23,330 --> 00:06:25,010
That's because the pace in high school
is different from

59
00:06:25,010 --> 00:06:25,870
middle school.

60
00:06:26,010 --> 00:06:27,180
Exams are just a way

61
00:06:27,370 --> 00:06:28,540
for us to assess students' proficiency

62
00:06:28,540 --> 00:06:29,860
at this stage.

63
00:06:31,930 --> 00:06:34,570
Jin Baihui is different from
other students.

64
00:06:34,860 --> 00:06:36,300
She came back from Beijing,

65
00:06:36,300 --> 00:06:37,690
s-so she should have adapted to

66
00:06:37,690 --> 00:06:40,100
this pace a year earlier than
most students.

67
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:41,220
Yes, that's right.

68
00:06:43,770 --> 00:06:45,370
I understand how you both feel.

69
00:06:45,370 --> 00:06:48,060
I'll also keep a close eye
on my students' progress

70
00:06:48,060 --> 00:06:49,659
from the teaching side.

71
00:06:50,010 --> 00:06:52,100
But at the same time, I hope parents

72
00:06:52,250 --> 00:06:53,250
can maintain

73
00:06:53,770 --> 00:06:55,100
a more relaxed mindset.

74
00:06:55,250 --> 00:06:56,620
Once an exam is over, it's over.

75
00:06:56,620 --> 00:06:58,080
We still have the next one.

76
00:06:58,100 --> 00:06:59,130
Besides, I think Jin Baihui

77
00:06:59,130 --> 00:07:00,770
is a well-rounded student.

78
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:03,550
I think you should have confidence in her.

79
00:07:05,570 --> 00:07:06,420
By the way, there's the school anniversary

80
00:07:06,420 --> 00:07:08,860
celebration this afternoon,
with performances.

81
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:10,660
She'll be going on stage as well.

82
00:07:15,220 --> 00:07:16,620
She'll be going on stage?

83
00:07:19,570 --> 00:07:20,970
She's the lead vocalist.

84
00:07:21,010 --> 00:07:22,620
The song their band will be performing

85
00:07:22,620 --> 00:07:23,890
was written by her.

86
00:07:24,100 --> 00:07:26,630
I heard them rehearse.
They were really good.

87
00:07:53,250 --> 00:07:54,909
Those lyrics from yesterday—

88
00:07:55,300 --> 00:07:57,360
you wrote them yourself, didn't you?

89
00:07:58,590 --> 00:08:00,920
And you're even going to perform
on stage?

90
00:08:01,180 --> 00:08:03,980
How could you keep
such an important thing from us?

91
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:07,520
Writing songs and rehearsing

92
00:08:07,540 --> 00:08:09,860
must have taken up
so much of your study time.

93
00:08:09,860 --> 00:08:11,060
Your grades have ended up like this

94
00:08:11,060 --> 00:08:12,930
because you've been putting your heart

95
00:08:12,930 --> 00:08:14,590
into these pointless things.

96
00:08:16,540 --> 00:08:18,870
Who cares about some school performance?

97
00:08:19,060 --> 00:08:22,460
Will it get you any extra points
on the college entrance exam?

98
00:08:23,540 --> 00:08:26,010
- Dad, I...
- Baihui.

99
00:08:26,660 --> 00:08:27,770
Your dad is right.

100
00:08:29,250 --> 00:08:32,010
What's the point of taking part in
some school performance?

101
00:08:32,010 --> 00:08:33,820
You only have so much time and energy.

102
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:35,220
If you waste it on things like this,

103
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:37,020
of course your grades will drop.

104
00:08:38,130 --> 00:08:40,100
How many times do I have to tell you?

105
00:08:40,130 --> 00:08:42,700
These little moments of happiness
you're chasing now

106
00:08:42,700 --> 00:08:45,560
will only become obstacles
on your path to success.

107
00:08:46,050 --> 00:08:46,740
You'd be better off spending that time

108
00:08:46,740 --> 00:08:48,740
doing a couple more practice tests.

109
00:08:54,770 --> 00:08:55,580
Be good

110
00:08:56,220 --> 00:08:57,550
and go tell your teacher

111
00:08:57,650 --> 00:08:59,510
that you won't be participating.

112
00:09:00,580 --> 00:09:02,860
Mom, this performance isn't just about me.

113
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:04,820
It's the hard work of
many other classmates, too.

114
00:09:04,820 --> 00:09:05,620
If I don't participate,

115
00:09:05,620 --> 00:09:06,890
it'll affect them all.

116
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:08,410
How am I supposed to
get along with them then?

117
00:09:08,410 --> 00:09:09,220
Get along?

118
00:09:10,170 --> 00:09:11,700
You don't need to get along with them.

119
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:13,700
You only need to come in first place.

120
00:09:15,820 --> 00:09:17,370
I know it's hard for you now,

121
00:09:17,820 --> 00:09:21,220
but sometimes you have to feel this pain
to learn your lesson.

122
00:09:21,410 --> 00:09:22,130
Mom.

123
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:23,770
About the school anniversary
this afternoon,

124
00:09:23,770 --> 00:09:25,650
go explain the situation
to your teacher yourself.

125
00:09:25,650 --> 00:09:26,980
Don't let us down again.

126
00:09:27,510 --> 00:09:28,410
Have you decided

127
00:09:28,410 --> 00:09:30,050
which ending pose you'll use?

128
00:09:30,050 --> 00:09:31,290
As long as it looks cool.

129
00:09:31,290 --> 00:09:32,330
That's for sure.

130
00:09:33,170 --> 00:09:33,830
Jin Baihui.

131
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:39,140
T-These must be your parents.

132
00:09:40,250 --> 00:09:42,110
Nice to meet you, Mr. and Mrs. Jin.

133
00:09:42,170 --> 00:09:43,820
Come and watch our performance
this afternoon.

134
00:09:43,820 --> 00:09:45,480
Jin Baihui sings really well.

135
00:09:46,650 --> 00:09:49,340
So you guys are in a band together, right?

136
00:09:50,170 --> 00:09:51,100
Yes...

137
00:09:51,370 --> 00:09:52,650
Let me tell you,

138
00:09:53,170 --> 00:09:54,130
my daughter Jin Baihui

139
00:09:54,130 --> 00:09:55,460
isn't interested in these things.

140
00:09:55,460 --> 00:09:56,530
- Dad.
- In the future,

141
00:09:56,530 --> 00:09:59,190
don't involve her in these activities
anymore.

142
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:24,740
[Pursue Knowledge, Seek Truth;
Practice Diligently, Foster Innovation]

143
00:10:28,740 --> 00:10:29,600
What happened?

144
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:33,640
What's wrong?

145
00:10:43,990 --> 00:10:45,620
[Pursue Knowledge, Seek Truth;
Practice Diligently, Foster Innovation]

146
00:10:56,340 --> 00:10:57,870
Lin Zhixia, Tang Tingting.

147
00:10:58,260 --> 00:10:59,260
Come out for a bit.

148
00:11:17,820 --> 00:11:20,480
Jin Baihui won't be performing
this afternoon.

149
00:11:20,820 --> 00:11:21,620
Why?

150
00:11:24,130 --> 00:11:25,100
Something came up.

151
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:26,900
I won't go into details with you.

152
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:28,410
If she's unable to perform,

153
00:11:28,410 --> 00:11:30,810
is there anyone else
who can take her place?

154
00:11:35,250 --> 00:11:37,110
Her throat hasn't recovered yet.

155
00:11:38,700 --> 00:11:40,630
If there's no one to take her place,

156
00:11:41,940 --> 00:11:44,600
the school may have to
cancel this performance.

157
00:11:48,740 --> 00:11:49,940
Ms. Kong, I can sing.

158
00:11:50,130 --> 00:11:51,740
Please don't cancel our performance.

159
00:11:51,740 --> 00:11:52,530
Are you sure?

160
00:11:55,740 --> 00:11:56,460
Alright then.

161
00:11:56,460 --> 00:11:57,770
I'll try to help you.

162
00:11:58,170 --> 00:11:59,820
But you have to be prepared.

163
00:12:06,050 --> 00:12:07,500
Is our performance going through
some kind of ordeal?

164
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:09,100
Do we have to face 81 trials?

165
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:10,150
Am I Tang Sanzang or something?

166
00:12:10,150 --> 00:12:11,180
Save your voice.

167
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:24,360
[Reading Corner]

168
00:12:24,380 --> 00:12:25,640
What could I say?

169
00:12:26,360 --> 00:12:29,590
[Reading Corner]

170
00:12:32,700 --> 00:12:34,360
It's about Jin Baihui, right?

171
00:12:35,770 --> 00:12:37,740
We just ran into her parents.

172
00:12:38,220 --> 00:12:40,150
I thought my dad was fierce enough,

173
00:12:40,740 --> 00:12:43,670
but Jin Baihui's parents were both
on another level.

174
00:12:44,010 --> 00:12:45,580
What's wrong with her parents?

175
00:12:45,580 --> 00:12:47,860
Her parents wouldn't let her
perform this afternoon,

176
00:12:47,860 --> 00:12:50,320
saying it would distract her
from studying.

177
00:12:50,820 --> 00:12:52,130
I guess to them,

178
00:12:52,410 --> 00:12:54,070
anything other than studying

179
00:12:54,220 --> 00:12:55,750
is considered rebellious.

180
00:12:57,170 --> 00:13:00,220
S-Should we encourage her to be
a little rebellious this time?

181
00:13:00,220 --> 00:13:02,060
My voice still isn't back to normal,

182
00:13:02,060 --> 00:13:04,320
and this song was written by Jin Baihui.

183
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:05,700
I haven't practiced it enough,

184
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:07,830
so I really don't have the confidence.

185
00:13:08,370 --> 00:13:09,220
Forget it.

186
00:13:09,890 --> 00:13:11,980
You guys didn't see the way
Jin Baihui's dad

187
00:13:11,980 --> 00:13:14,530
shoved this program sheet at me.

188
00:13:16,580 --> 00:13:19,130
I feel like if she goes against them
and performs,

189
00:13:19,130 --> 00:13:21,330
her parents might actually beat her up.

190
00:13:26,050 --> 00:13:26,700
Tingting.

191
00:13:26,980 --> 00:13:28,500
Take some throat lozenges right away

192
00:13:28,500 --> 00:13:30,980
and try to get your voice in better shape
before you go on stage.

193
00:13:30,980 --> 00:13:32,580
You'll be able to pull it off.

194
00:13:45,370 --> 00:13:46,740
Distinguished leaders,

195
00:13:46,740 --> 00:13:47,700
honored guests,

196
00:13:47,740 --> 00:13:49,890
dear teachers and students,

197
00:13:50,010 --> 00:13:51,500
I hereby declare

198
00:13:51,530 --> 00:13:54,740
the 50th Anniversary Celebration
of Nanhai Province No. 1 High School

199
00:13:54,740 --> 00:13:55,770
officially open.

200
00:14:02,620 --> 00:14:03,940
Up next is a performance

201
00:14:03,940 --> 00:14:07,050
brought to you by Class 4, Grade 10
—a flute solo of "La Traviata."

202
00:14:07,050 --> 00:14:08,290
Please enjoy.

203
00:14:08,900 --> 00:14:11,800
[United in Glory,
Building a Brilliant Campus Together]

204
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:09,780
♪ The evening breeze rustles the willows
as the flute's melody fades ♪

205
00:15:09,810 --> 00:15:15,590
♪ The setting sun sets
beyond the mountains ♪

206
00:15:38,260 --> 00:15:40,380
[Notice Board]

207
00:15:42,390 --> 00:15:43,650
Are you really willing

208
00:15:44,220 --> 00:15:45,620
to give up just like that?

209
00:15:51,410 --> 00:15:53,210
This song is your original work.

210
00:15:53,340 --> 00:15:55,870
No one else can bring it to life
the way you can.

211
00:15:57,940 --> 00:15:59,010
There are so many performances
at the anniversary celebration.

212
00:15:59,010 --> 00:16:00,580
It won't matter if there's one less,
right?

213
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:02,370
We've been rehearsing together
for so long.

214
00:16:02,370 --> 00:16:04,230
How can you just give up like that?

215
00:16:08,100 --> 00:16:09,010
My parents asked me

216
00:16:09,010 --> 00:16:11,740
to finish these 3 practice tests
this afternoon.

217
00:16:24,460 --> 00:16:25,990
Have you ever thought about

218
00:16:26,580 --> 00:16:27,440
taking a break?

219
00:16:39,050 --> 00:16:40,340
Next, please enjoy

220
00:16:40,340 --> 00:16:41,770
the classical dance performed by
the students of Class 2, Grade 10,

221
00:16:41,770 --> 00:16:44,370
"Ode to the Orchid Pavilion."

222
00:17:11,089 --> 00:17:12,480
Bravo!

223
00:17:28,980 --> 00:17:29,940
Come on, guys.

224
00:17:30,150 --> 00:17:32,480
We have no choice but to go for it.
Let's go!

225
00:17:35,960 --> 00:17:37,070
Up next

226
00:17:37,180 --> 00:17:39,140
is a song performed by Class 1, Grade 10.

227
00:17:39,140 --> 00:17:40,610
This one is truly amazing.

228
00:17:41,050 --> 00:17:43,520
The band is made up of members
from the first- and second-place teams

229
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:45,180
in the previous math contest.

230
00:17:45,590 --> 00:17:47,110
Are you excited to see them?

231
00:17:47,110 --> 00:17:48,480
Yes!

232
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:50,750
Next, please enjoy "Closed Loop."

233
00:17:58,320 --> 00:18:01,730
[United in Glory,
Building a Brilliant Campus Together]

234
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:04,910
[Nanhai No. 1 High School Anniversary]

235
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:19,510
[United in Glory,
Building a Brilliant Campus Together]

236
00:18:19,530 --> 00:18:22,740
[Nanhai No. 1 High School Anniversary]

237
00:18:29,530 --> 00:18:30,500
♪ Waiting ♪

238
00:18:30,900 --> 00:18:35,140
♪ Enduring every second ♪

239
00:18:50,350 --> 00:18:53,280
[United in Glory,
Building a Brilliant Campus Together]

240
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:56,960
[Nanhai No. 1 High School Anniversary]

241
00:19:11,740 --> 00:19:12,700
♪ Waiting ♪

242
00:19:13,010 --> 00:19:17,140
♪ Enduring every second ♪

243
00:19:35,460 --> 00:19:35,990
Let's go.

244
00:19:52,810 --> 00:19:53,610
Jin Baihui.

245
00:19:55,610 --> 00:19:57,700
Not everyone has a talent like yours—

246
00:19:59,380 --> 00:20:00,510
that kind of ability

247
00:20:02,330 --> 00:20:04,010
which can bring notes to life.

248
00:20:05,500 --> 00:20:06,940
Your parents might say no,

249
00:20:06,940 --> 00:20:08,600
but don't give up on yourself.

250
00:20:10,980 --> 00:20:12,140
Because hidden within the notes you write

251
00:20:12,140 --> 00:20:14,250
are the words
you're too afraid to say out loud.

252
00:20:14,250 --> 00:20:15,330
Your songs and your words

253
00:20:15,330 --> 00:20:17,330
deserve to be heard again and again.

254
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:19,980
This performance

255
00:20:19,980 --> 00:20:22,050
is like a 10-minute break between classes—

256
00:20:22,050 --> 00:20:24,140
a precious 10 minutes

257
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:26,250
you might not encounter
very often in life.

258
00:20:26,250 --> 00:20:27,530
When the break is over,

259
00:20:27,700 --> 00:20:29,050
we'll all return to our normal lives

260
00:20:29,050 --> 00:20:30,050
and schoolwork.

261
00:20:31,290 --> 00:20:33,020
Are you sure you want to miss out

262
00:20:33,190 --> 00:20:36,520
on a memory that might stay with you
for the rest of your life?

263
00:20:41,290 --> 00:20:42,820
The band is waiting for you.

264
00:20:56,900 --> 00:20:59,360
Let's go on stage together,
take that break,

265
00:20:59,530 --> 00:21:00,530
and then return to

266
00:21:01,250 --> 00:21:02,780
our normal lives together.

267
00:21:03,570 --> 00:21:04,250
Okay?

268
00:21:46,130 --> 00:21:46,860
♪ Waiting ♪

269
00:21:47,620 --> 00:21:51,390
♪ Every second is a test of endurance ♪

270
00:21:52,290 --> 00:21:53,090
♪ Run away quickly ♪

271
00:21:53,770 --> 00:21:57,240
♪ Testing with ulterior motives ♪

272
00:21:57,620 --> 00:21:59,130
♪ If I could start over ♪

273
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:04,080
♪ Why not now? ♪

274
00:22:04,720 --> 00:22:05,450
♪ It will turn around ♪

275
00:22:06,590 --> 00:22:09,290
♪ Create accidents for accidents ♪

276
00:22:09,860 --> 00:22:12,910
♪ Break out all the fake love ♪

277
00:22:13,460 --> 00:22:16,100
♪ This dangerous persona ♪

278
00:22:16,500 --> 00:22:19,090
♪ Please shut off your sense of
smell and sight ♪

279
00:22:19,310 --> 00:22:21,850
♪ Your hearing and touch ♪

280
00:22:22,270 --> 00:22:25,350
♪ Break out all the fake love ♪

281
00:22:25,890 --> 00:22:28,450
♪ Who made the rules? ♪

282
00:22:28,840 --> 00:22:31,240
♪ Not loving is the most alluring thing ♪

283
00:22:31,500 --> 00:22:34,200
♪ It's my turn this time ♪

284
00:22:34,530 --> 00:22:35,330
It's the school anniversary after all.

285
00:22:35,130 --> 00:22:36,340
♪ Who's the one waiting? ♪

286
00:22:36,380 --> 00:22:37,380
The atmosphere is what matters most.

287
00:22:37,250 --> 00:22:41,010
♪ The hunter takes on the guise
of the prey ♪

288
00:22:37,770 --> 00:22:38,500
The students in our class

289
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:40,560
really know how to pull off anything.

290
00:22:41,890 --> 00:22:42,530
♪ There's no escape ♪

291
00:22:43,360 --> 00:22:46,840
♪ From these familiar tactics ♪

292
00:22:47,360 --> 00:22:48,850
♪ It's too late to surrender ♪

293
00:22:50,020 --> 00:22:53,670
♪ A love that can never fall into sync ♪

294
00:22:54,170 --> 00:22:54,990
♪ Another twist ♪

295
00:22:56,010 --> 00:22:58,760
♪ We've formed a closed loop ♪

296
00:22:56,720 --> 00:22:58,250
Let's get this party going!

297
00:22:59,450 --> 00:23:02,680
♪ Break out all the fake love ♪

298
00:23:02,990 --> 00:23:05,720
♪ This dangerous persona ♪

299
00:23:06,130 --> 00:23:08,690
♪ Please shut off your sense of
smell and sight ♪

300
00:23:08,920 --> 00:23:11,520
♪ Your hearing and touch ♪

301
